{
  "type": "quotient-flow-panel",
  "label": "Quotient flow — step settings panel",
  "category": "mockups",
  "description": "The Quotient flow editor's side panel: a selected step's settings, in the product's look (Edit / Analytics / History tabs, sections of labelled fields: dropdowns, text fields, notes, radio choices). Pair it with quotient-flow -- panel beside the diagram reads as the editor -- to show HOW a step is set up: the trigger type picked, the audience chosen, an email chosen for a branch. Two views: `settings` (the step's fields) and `add-step` (the step picker: a grid of step types -- Delay, Send Email, Conditional, AI Email, Update Person, Update Lead Score, Send to CRM, Notify User, Send Slack Message, HTTP Request, Agent). Scriptable: `type` a value into a field (a caret, character by character), `select` an option (dropdown value swaps, radio moves), `highlight` a field with a ring, `view` switch views, `pick` a step type in the picker (hover, press, ring). 'Add step -> pick Send Email -> its settings' is view add-step, pick, view settings. Every `at` takes a word anchor. With no sections it shows the real trigger panel. Designed 350 wide; give it a tall narrow box (about 350x580 proportions).",
